  "discovered_via": "manufacturer product page link list, fetched 2026-10-09",
  "summary": "Dual-channel (half-bridge) isolated gate-driver board for 1700 V SiC modules and discretes: two TI UCC21710 drivers with DESAT overcurrent detection through two series US3M high-voltage diodes, 400 mA soft turn-off, Miller clamp, UVLO/RDY and isolated analog-to-PWM thermistor channel; RS-422 differential inputs (SN65C1167), global fault combining, per-channel 2 W isolated SIP DC/DC module with input common-mode choke and optional LDO post-regulation; input reverse-polarity P-FET and 20 V Zener clamp.",
  "license": {
    "redistribution": "not-verified",
    "terms_source": "document footers and Important Notes (PRD-06992 pp.36-37)",
    "notes": "Wolfspeed documents carry '(c) Wolfspeed, Inc. All rights reserved'; no redistribution licence was found in the documents or design-file archives inspected. Treated as not redistributable; only original analysis and metadata are committed."
  },
  "evidence_limitations": [
    "The OrCAD/Allegro sources are from 2020-2023 while the BOM workbook was updated in October 2025; component values differ between the Rev V1 schematic PDF (e.g. LDO divider 10 k / 2.2 k, DB4 STPS2150A) and the 2025 BOM (54.9 k / 12.1 k, SK215A). Both negative-LDO dividers evaluate to about -4.0 V.",
    "Connectivity claims for the DESAT and gate paths were confirmed against the Allegro expanded netlist (pstxnet.dat, 2020-06-23); the Allegro .brd file was not parsed.",
    "Creepage figures quoted in PRD-09301 Figure 20 are graphical and were not extracted numerically.",
    "No switching measurements of this board are published in the user guide; electrical characteristics are stated as typical values at 25 degC with RG(EXT) = 1 ohm and 47 nF load."
  ],
  "analysis": "analysis.md",
  "ratings": {
    "supply_voltage": "10.8-13.2 V (12 V typ.)",
    "dc_bus": "up to 1500 V (user guide section 2)",
    "output_levels": "+15/-3 V (-UNA), +15/-4 V (-R1), +18/-4 V (-R2)",
    "peak_output_current": "+/-10 A",
    "power_per_channel": "2 W",
    "max_switching_frequency": "1 MHz (driver IC limit; gate-charge dependent)",
    "working_isolation": "1500 Vrms; CMTI 150 kV/us min",
    "board_size": "50.8 x 59.69 mm, 4 layers, 1.6 mm FR4"
  },
  "source_discrepancies": [
    "Input connector JT1 is SBH11-PBPC-D08-ST-BK in the BOM and schematic but SBH11-NBPC-D08-SM-BK in user-guide Table 5.",
    "User-guide note 1 to Table 11: the schematic text names MGJ2D121505SC for +15 V/-4 V while the document and BOM use MGJ2D122005SC with LDO post-regulation.",
    "Schematic sheet notes 'OC threshold for shutdown is 0.7 V' and 'Vf of the two high voltage diodes is roughly ~1 V' (total); the user guide uses 0.5 V per diode - consistent in total.",
    "Board specification files name the PCB 'CGD1700HB2M-FM3 Rev A' and the Allegro file 'CGD1700GB2M-UNA Rev A.brd' (typo in source)."
  ]
}
